    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$3.52 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for a burrito bowl the fast casual chains price at $12 before extras. Each of these costs less than a third of one of theirs.",
    "shop_smart":  ["Jarred salsa is the flavor engine, and it replaces tomatoes, chiles, and half your spice rack in one pour. Store brand jars on sale drop the cost further.","The 4 lb pack of 93/7 ground turkey is the price-per-pound winner, and this recipe uses 3.75 lb of it, so nothing lingers in the fridge.","Seasoned black beans are cheap by the can and add protein and fiber for next to nothing a bowl. Stock up when they hit a sale price."],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Cook the rice: rinse, simmer covered with water until tender, and set aside.",
                    "Heat the olive oil in your biggest skillet. Cook the diced red onion and green bell peppers until soft, about 6 minutes, then add the garlic for 1 minute.",
                    "Add the ground turkey and break it up as it browns. Cook to 165F with no pink remaining, then stir in the taco seasoning, salt, and black pepper.",
                    "Pour in the salsa and simmer 8 to 10 minutes until it thickens into a saucy taco filling.",
                    "Stir in the drained black beans and heat through.",
                    "Portion rice into 14 containers, top with the turkey mixture, then finish with cheese and chopped cilantro."
                ],
